* sg13g2-pll :: sim/sg13cmos5l-vco-period-jitter (issue #518, Part of #16)
* Calibration stage: ONE vco_stage from the frozen snapshot, biased in its
* high-gain linear region at a stable DC operating point -- the circuit the
* injected-noise amplitude is calibrated against (RECORD-001
* "Calibration").  Bias: VBP/VBN held by ideal sources at the values
* tb_bias_op measured for this operating point; the stage input self-biases
* to its own DC trip point through Rfb=1e12 (XMP/XMN currents balance
* exactly, zero current through Rfb), so the linear-region bias point is
* the circuit's own solution, not a hand-picked voltage.
*
* This deck: .op (the self-bias solution, printed) + .noise at the stage
* output over 100 kHz..100 GHz -> the true small-signal device-noise output
* spectral density the injected source must reproduce in-band.  The
* reference source for input-referred noise is vbiasp (ac 1); onoise does
* not depend on that choice.
*
* Template placeholders: @VBP@/@VBN@ (from tb_bias_op), plus the shared
* @CORNER_MOS@/@CORNER_RES@/@TEMP@/@PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@/@OSDI@ set.
.lib @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerMOShv.lib @CORNER_MOS@
.lib @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerRES.lib @CORNER_RES@
.option scale=1 temp=@TEMP@
.global sub!
.include vco_open.spice
vbiasp vbp 0 dc @VBP@ ac 1
vbiasn vbn 0 dc @VBN@
vdd vdd 0 dc 3.3
vsub sub! 0 dc 0
xs1 sin1 vbp vbn sout vdd 0 vco_stage
rfb sout sin1 1e12
.control
pre_osdi @OSDI@/psp103.osdi
pre_osdi @OSDI@/psp103_nqs.osdi
pre_osdi @OSDI@/mosvar.osdi
pre_osdi @OSDI@/r3_cmc.osdi
op
set numdgt=15
print v(sin1) v(sout)
* pts-per-summary 1: creates the noise1 (spectral-density) and noise2
* (integrated, per-device) plots the prints below read
noise v(sout) vbiasp dec 20 1e5 1e11 1
setplot noise1
print frequency onoise_spectrum
setplot noise2
print all
.endc
.end
